columns named under "Not under CC BY-SA" below.

  Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
  Summary:    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The files are DERIVED / MODIFIED from these DoltHub databases, which declare
the same licence (each repo has a LICENSE.md titled "Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International"):

  - https://www.dolthub.com/repositories/post-no-preference/earnings
  - https://www.dolthub.com/repositories/post-no-preference/options

and, for the company names, GICS sectors and CIKs in security.parquet, from
Wikipedia, "List of S&P 500 companies", revision 1382178819 (CC BY-SA 4.0).

Attribution: the original data is from DoltHub, repositories
post-no-preference/earnings and post-no-preference/options, and from
Wikipedia. We selected and filtered it (see the code in src/ and tools/ that
makes each file). We changed the data; DoltHub, Wikipedia and the original
authors do not endorse the changes.

ShareAlike: if you remix or build on these files, you must share your
version under CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a compatible licence) as well.

Not under CC BY-SA (owner decision of 2026-10-29: real values the app and the
docs need may be committed). These columns are derived from Yahoo Finance
prices or from the Cboe VIX index and fall under those providers' terms, not
under CC BY-SA. Two are derived from Yahoo Finance prices (Yahoo's terms of
service):

  - timing_check.parquet, column gap_verdict_yf: the verdict of the Yahoo
    overnight price gap on the timing label in use (supports, contradicts,
    quiet). The app's sample_funnel.json carries a share built from it.
  - security.parquet, column in_universe: which 50 companies the study keeps,
    chosen by a one-time Yahoo market-cap rank (the rank itself is not here).

Since milestone 4, results.parquet also holds regression coefficients of SIZE
(ln market cap at day -1, built from the rank date's Yahoo market cap and
Yahoo closes; the per-event values stay local): Yahoo's terms, not CC BY-SA.
And event_measures.parquet holds vix_regime, a three-level label (low, mid,
high) of the Cboe VIX close at day -1, cut at terciles within each sample:
Cboe's terms, not CC BY-SA. The other milestone-4 columns of
event_measures.parquet (price_ref, surprise_scaled, abs_surprise_scaled_w,
sue_hist, sue_hist_n) come from the DoltHub option forwards and EPS history
and stay under CC BY-SA.

FRED: no column here is a FRED value. The IVs, variances and moves in
iv_daily.parquet and event_iv.parquet are computed from the DoltHub option
quotes with FRED's DTB3 rate as an input (the discount factor and the carry);
they stay under CC BY-SA as above. DTB3 is public domain; FRED asks for this
citation: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (US), 3-Month
Treasury Bill Secondary Market Rate, Discount Basis [DTB3], retrieved from
FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis; https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DTB3,
2026-10-29.

Cboe VIX (milestone 3): results.parquet holds statistics computed with the
VIX close, which FRED republishes from Cboe as VIXCLS (Cboe copyright). The
numbers of its market-adjusted rows (adjustment = market: estimate, se, stat,
p_value, ci_lo, ci_hi, p_holm, q_bh, rbar) and of gate G1's rows (family =
validation, among them the calibration rows g1_calibration:* and
g1_calibration_sigma_d:*) are aggregates over many VIX-adjusted values and
fall under Cboe's terms, not under CC BY-SA. Two of the calibration rows are
named here because they are statistics of VIX itself or of the VIX betas:
dm_sd, the standard deviation of the daily change of ln VIX over the study
period, and beta_median, the median over the 50 companies of their VIX beta.
They are committed under the owner's decision of 2026-10-29 (ADR 0001 §7:
commit the real data the apps and docs need, including Cboe values). FRED asks for this citation: Chicago Board Options Exchange,
CBOE Volatility Index: VIX [VIXCLS], retrieved from FRED, Federal Reserve
Bank of St. Louis; https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/VIXCLS, 2026-10-29.
No VIX value, and no per-event or per-company VIX-adjusted value, is in this
folder: event_window_obs and event_measures hold only the mean-adjusted
values (the VIX-adjusted columns, names ending in _cboe, stay local).

Outside this folder, docs/milestones/03-event-study.md §6.5 quotes further
Cboe-derived aggregates under the same decision (ADR 0001 §7) and the same
terms: the median, minimum and maximum company VIX beta (the minimum and
the maximum are each one unnamed company's beta), and six named per-company
firm-cluster terms of the VIX-adjusted RUNUP and PERSIST_10 (the sum over one
company's events of its deviations from the mean). The root DATA.md lists
them. Since milestone 4, docs/milestones/04-drivers.md §6.6 and
research/prototypes/rhobar_crush.out.txt quote per-date aggregates of the
standardised VIX-adjusted crush-baseline changes on 10 named dates
(2025-11-24, 2026-06-05, 2024-12-19, 2026-03-09, 2026-03-10, 2024-12-18,
2026-06-08, 2025-03-10, 2025-03-14, 2025-06-23): each date's mean and mean
pair product over 31 to 41 companies, under the same decision and terms.

Also outside this folder, app/public/data/implied_vs_realised.json (milestone
4) has 336 per-event rows built from event_measures.parquet, events.parquet
and security.parquet here: the implied move at day -1 and the realised day-0
move r0, both from the DoltHub option quotes (r0 is the option-forward return
realized_ret_0, not a Yahoo return), the scaled surprise and the GICS sector.
It is derived from the DoltHub and Wikipedia data above and is shared under
CC BY-SA 4.0 on the same terms, under the owner's decision of 2026-10-29
(ADR 0001 §7).

Cboe VX*: no VX* value is in this folder or anywhere else in this
repository. security.parquet's cboe_vx_index only names the Cboe index that
exists for a company (VXAPL and four others); it holds no index value.

The timing labels (events.parquet) are not derived from Yahoo data: they come
from the DoltHub calendar and from company press releases. A Yahoo price gap
only decides which events are looked up or read a second time (data model
§2.1, class F).

The licence of the rest of this repository (the code) is the MIT licence in
the LICENSE file at the root of the repository. It does not apply to this
folder. The root DATA.md says what each source's terms restrict.
